A Web Application Firewall (WAF) is an appliance or software that monitors HTTP/HTTPS traffic and can block malicious traffic
to and from web application, WAFs target content from specific web applications at the application level, while
edge firewalls from secure gateways between the local area network (LAN) and outside servers at the network level

By inspecting HTTP traffic, WAFs can stop attacks originating from web application security flaws such as:
- SQL injection
- Cross-site scripting
- File inclusion
- Security misconfigurations

developed in the 90s, the WAFs ancestor was a largely network-based firewall, it can target File transfer protocol (FTP)
Remote shell (RSH)

